REQ-04 / AC-04 require preserved immediate predecessors and reexamination of
affected documentary criteria without rerunning unrelated product observations.

## Operational closure work authorized 2026-11-02

The maintainer now authorizes local inventory, measurement, instrumentation, tests,
bounded foundation fixes and affected SDD updates. This supersedes documentary-only
execution restrictions above for this follow-up, not the historical observations.
No commits, publication, global installation, remote agents, storage implementation
or roadmap expansion. F0-D1..D5 adoption remains a separate explicit decision.

- REQ-05: Execute the applicable F0-P01..P07 and Q01..Q13 contract using current observations; distinguish adoption, implementation and acceptance.
- AC-05 → REQ-05: Every applicable F0 clause has current adequate evidence and an APPROVED or justified NOT APPLICABLE verdict, including adopted measurement limits; pending decisions, absent evidence, failures and skips prevent closure.

Cancellation investigation: controlled direct children must be reaped before terminal
cancellation is reported; cancelled verification cannot approve. Check actual work,
not only a cancellation flag. Subprocess deadlines do not guarantee bounded filesystem
I/O or total-operation duration. Preserve existing API callers where possible.
